<title>USA: SulAmerica unit sells $40 mln of Eurobonds.</title>
<headline>SulAmerica unit sells $40 mln of Eurobonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following Eurobond issue from SulAmerica International Bank (Cayman Ltd) was priced on Wednesday, according to lead manager Credit Lyonnais.</p>
<p>The issuer is an offshore subsidiary of SulAmerica de Seguros SA, a Brazilian insurance company.</p>
<p>BORROWER SULAMERICA INTERNATIONAL BANK (CAYMAN LTD)</p>
<p>AMT $40 MLN	  COUPON 9.3 PCT    MATURITY 2/14/2000</p>
<p>TYPE EUROBOND	ISS PRICE 99.8718 FIRST PAY DATE 8/14/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S NR    YIELD 9.35 PCT    PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P NR	  SPREAD 320 BPS    CALLABLE NON-CALLABLE</p>
<p>NOTES: -SECURITIES PAY IN U.S. DOLLARS</p>
<p>	 -APPLICATION TO BE MADE FOR LISTING ON LUXEMBOURG</p>
<p>	     EXCHANGE</p>
<p>	 -U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1662</p>
